# Remelle theme conventions

## Accordions / expands

- Every `<details>` accordion starts **closed**.
- Never set `open` / `open: true` by default in templates, `settings_data.json`, or section presets.
- An optional theme-editor checkbox to open a row is fine; default it to `false`.

## Editable copy

- Customer-facing text must be editable in Shopify (theme editor section/block settings, or locale keys via Edit default theme content).
- Do not hardcode English strings in Liquid markup.
- Prefer section/block `text` / `richtext` / `textarea` settings for page and section copy.
- Use `{{ 'key' | t }}` only for shared chrome/UI strings that belong in locale files.
- Schema `default` values are starting copy only; merchants override them in the theme editor.

## Account / contact

- Guest Account uses `routes.account_url` (Shopify hosted accounts).
- Contact form submissions go to the store Sender email; display `info@remelle.shop` in theme settings.

## Hide / delete sections

- Never lock sections with static `{% section %}` in `layout/` or `templates/`.
- Use `{% sections 'header-group' %}` / `{% sections 'footer-group' %}` in the layout.
- Page and template content must live in JSON templates so merchants can hide or remove sections in the theme editor.
- Every customer-facing section needs a schema `presets` entry so it can be added back after removal.
